Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.19,0:00:02.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,The difference between one and eight is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.57,0:00:02.93,Cap,,0,0,0,,seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.09,0:00:04.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,The difference between eight and 27 is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.85,0:00:05.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,19.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.55,0:00:07.17,Cap,,0,0,0,,The difference between 27 is 37.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.73,0:00:10.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,However, the difference between seven and 19
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.39,0:00:10.99,Cap,,0,0,0,,is 12.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.43,0:00:14.01,Cap,,0,0,0,,The difference between 37 and 19 is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.01,0:00:14.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,18.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.99,0:00:16.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,Guess what's going to happen if I
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.13,0:00:18.71,Cap,,0,0,0,,do 125 minus 64 and I ask
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.71,0:00:19.95,Cap,,0,0,0,,for the difference, it's going to be
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.95,0:00:20.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,24.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.77,0:00:21.81,Cap,,0,0,0,,Are you seeing where this is going?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.21,0:00:23.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is going to be changing by
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.67,0:00:24.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,multiples of six.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.17,0:00:26.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,Do you see what I'm getting at?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.99,0:00:29.89,Cap,,0,0,0,,So here's the point, because this is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.89,0:00:31.85,Cap,,0,0,0,,actually very interesting introduction to calculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.55,0:00:35.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,When you square a number, you will
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.61,0:00:37.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,find out that there's a pattern in
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.31,0:00:38.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,the difference between the squares.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.09,0:00:39.47,Cap,,0,0,0,,Are you seeing?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.01,0:00:40.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,There's a pattern.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.21,0:00:42.31,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now you could play with this later.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.43,0:00:43.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,You see what I mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.75,0:00:45.35,Cap,,0,0,0,,When you cube a number,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.59,0:00:49.57,Cap,,0,0,0,,there's a difference between those numbers, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.15,0:00:52.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,But there's a difference of the difference,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.21,0:00:53.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,which is where we get the 12,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.73,0:00:54.55,Cap,,0,0,0,,the 18 and the 24.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.99,0:00:56.19,Cap,,0,0,0,,And then if you do the math
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.19,0:00:57.09,Cap,,0,0,0,,further, guess what?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.19,0:00:58.39,Cap,,0,0,0,,The difference is going to become six.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.59,0:01:01.27,Cap,,0,0,0,,So here's the point in calculus.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.27,0:01:02.91,Cap,,0,0,0,,So I discovered this a few years
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.91,0:01:04.61,Cap,,0,0,0,,ago when I was teaching this topic
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.61,0:01:06.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,and I thought I had discovered something
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.87,0:01:09.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,nobody had done, but that is actually
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.03,0:01:09.67,Cap,,0,0,0,,kind of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.81,0:01:15.05,Cap,,0,0,0,,because Newton discovered it in the 1680s.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.67,0:01:16.93,Cap,,0,0,0,,And I don't know that he discovered
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.93,0:01:19.13,Cap,,0,0,0,,it within this context alone, but he
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.13,0:01:21.87,Cap,,0,0,0,,discovered a formula that tells you what
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.87,0:01:23.51,Cap,,0,0,0,,this number will be at the end
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.51,0:01:24.03,Cap,,0,0,0,,of the day.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.27,0:01:24.75,Cap,,0,0,0,,I don't know if you see what
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.75,0:01:24.97,Cap,,0,0,0,,I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.06,0:01:27.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,So like over the weekend, play with
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.24,0:01:27.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.50,0:01:27.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,I'm serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.06,0:01:29.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,You're going to notice something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.62,0:01:31.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,Find the difference of the numbers and
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.38,0:01:32.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,then find the difference of the difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.94,0:01:34.12,Cap,,0,0,0,,Once you do it for the fourth
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.12,0:01:35.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,power, guess what?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.52,0:01:37.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,You are now in calculus territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.84,0:01:40.26,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's literally, you've gone into calculus territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.96,0:01:42.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,And the reason why this is quite
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.06,0:01:44.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,fascinating is because what Newton showed us,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.86,0:01:48.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,guys, is that you can find what
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.74,0:01:50.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,that difference of the difference is without
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.92,0:01:52.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,manually doing what we're doing right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.90,0:01:53.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's what Newton did.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.26,0:01:54.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,Isn't that crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.52,0:01:57.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,You can actually, I can tell you
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.00,0:01:58.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,what the difference of the difference of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.98,0:02:00.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,the difference will be if we were
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.58,0:02:01.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,doing it like X to the 10th
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.90,0:02:02.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,power.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.40,0:02:02.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,Does that make sense?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.08,0:02:04.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,I don't have to actually do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.90,0:02:06.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's the beauty of mathematics, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.16,0:02:08.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,It creates pathways.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.34,0:02:11.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,And that's why it's just like, I
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.72,0:02:14.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,wish people understood what math is.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.04,0:02:16.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,Like I wish people understood what it
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.42,0:02:17.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,does to your thinking.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.92,0:02:19.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,Like I just wish they could.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.60,0:02:22.06,Cap,,0,0,0,,But then sometimes our education system just
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.06,0:02:22.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,makes it boring.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.18,0:02:24.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,And everybody's like, why am I doing
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.34,0:02:24.58,Cap,,0,0,0,,this?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.10,0:02:25.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,Because it's
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.20,0:02:27.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,Well, you guys have worked hard today.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.84,0:02:29.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,I should tell you one thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.20,0:02:30.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,I actually just let you see the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.70,0:02:31.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.60,0:02:32.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,Here's the secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.40,0:02:34.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Do you remember when we did the
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.68,0:02:35.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,squares?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.54,0:02:36.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,When we did x squared?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.18,0:02:39.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,What was the difference of the difference?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.34,0:02:40.08,Cap,,0,0,0,,What was that number?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.30,0:02:42.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,What was that constant number that was
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.02,0:02:42.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,occurring?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.04,0:02:43.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,Wasn't it two?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.08,0:02:45.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,Do you remember?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.20,0:02:46.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.96,0:02:49.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,In calculus, there's an idea that you
Dialogue: 0,0:02:49.80,0:02:52.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,can take this number here, and you
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.42,0:02:53.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,can bring it to the front.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.16,0:02:57.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,And then you can subtract by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.36,0:02:57.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.76,0:03:00.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,And the answer becomes 2x.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.58,0:03:02.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's the answer to, this is what
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.42,0:03:04.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,I just did, is called the derivative.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.20,0:03:06.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,So today I'm giving you a little
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.48,0:03:08.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,bit of kind of looking ahead for
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.40,0:03:08.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.00,0:03:09.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's called what?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.12,0:03:10.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,A derivative.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.80,0:03:12.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,We just took a derivative of x
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.30,0:03:12.52,Cap,,0,0,0,,squared.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.92,0:03:14.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,The way you take a derivative is
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.14,0:03:15.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,you take the number on the front,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.32,0:03:16.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,you bring it down, and then you
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.80,0:03:18.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,subtract the power up here by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.60,0:03:19.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Make sense?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.26,0:03:19.62,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.76,0:03:20.56,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's all you do.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.02,0:03:22.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now, guess what?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.68,0:03:25.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,That number reminds you of something.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.66,0:03:26.82,Cap,,0,0,0,,What does it remind you of?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.88,0:03:29.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,It reminds you of this over here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.10,0:03:31.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.80,0:03:32.34,Cap,,0,0,0,,Do you see this?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.72,0:03:34.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,That's what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.00,0:03:38.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now, we're going to go down, and
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.32,0:03:38.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,guess what?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.14,0:03:40.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,Let's take 3 cubed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.98,0:03:42.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,I mean, let's take x cubed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.24,0:03:42.38,Cap,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.16,0:03:44.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Remember what the formula for the derivative
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.60,0:03:44.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,is.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.02,0:03:45.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,Bring this down to the front.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.02,0:03:46.42,Cap,,0,0,0,,Is that true?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.54,0:03:48.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,And do what to the power?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.02,0:03:49.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,Reduce it by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.86,0:03:50.36,Cap,,0,0,0,,Is that true?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.16,0:03:52.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,Is that what I just did?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.38,0:03:52.48,Cap,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.58,0:03:52.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,I didn't cheat.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.14,0:03:53.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,Okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.64,0:03:54.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,But here's what, here's something.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.16,0:03:56.74,Cap,,0,0,0,,We are not done because this number
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.74,0:03:57.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,is not yet one.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.70,0:03:59.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,You stop when this number is one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.10,0:04:02.24,Cap,,0,0,0,,So now bring this again to the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.24,0:04:02.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,front.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.10,0:04:05.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,So you get 2 times 3x, and
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.64,0:04:06.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,this is one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.50,0:04:07.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Do you see?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.12,0:04:08.02,Cap,,0,0,0,,And now we can stop, correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.72,0:04:10.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,The answer is 6x.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.66,0:04:13.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now, if I ask you, but how
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.60,0:04:14.64,Cap,,0,0,0,,do we know if we go to
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.64,0:04:16.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,the fourth power, what will that constant
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.86,0:04:17.54,Cap,,0,0,0,,number be?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.04,0:04:19.94,Cap,,0,0,0,,If it's x to the fourth, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.36,0:04:21.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Imagine you start with one, and then
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.68,0:04:22.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,2 times 2 times 2 times 2
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.92,0:04:25.44,Cap,,0,0,0,,is 16, and 3 times 3 times
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.44,0:04:26.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,3 times 3 is 81.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.10,0:04:27.78,Cap,,0,0,0,,Does that make sense?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.96,0:04:29.66,Cap,,0,0,0,,If you find the difference of the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.66,0:04:31.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,difference of the difference, guess what?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.48,0:04:33.20,Cap,,0,0,0,,It is 4x to the third.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.32,0:04:34.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,You bring the 3 again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.66,0:04:36.32,Cap,,0,0,0,,It's 12x to the second.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.76,0:04:38.98,Cap,,0,0,0,,You bring the 2 down, and the
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.98,0:04:40.18,Cap,,0,0,0,,answer is 24, guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.82,0:04:42.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,That number that will be the constant
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.92,0:04:43.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,will be 24.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.38,0:04:44.92,Cap,,0,0,0,,Isn't that crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.30,0:04:46.28,Cap,,0,0,0,,Like, I know it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.30,0:04:47.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,I don't even have to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.26,0:04:48.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,I just know it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.04,0:04:49.72,Cap,,0,0,0,,And so that's what I discovered.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.98,0:04:52.50,Cap,,0,0,0,,I discovered the difference of the difference.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.62,0:04:54.16,Cap,,0,0,0,,I discovered that just personally.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.68,0:04:56.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,But then, as I started digging into
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.86,0:04:57.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,the calculus implication,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.64,0:05:00.90,Cap,,0,0,0,,I realized that's kind of what, like
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.90,0:05:02.14,Cap,,0,0,0,,Newton, that's the point.
